@moduledoc """
The rate limiter behind `<%= inspect(@web) %>.Plugs.RateLimit`: Hammer with its ETS backend,
supervised by the application.

    <%= inspect(@prefix) %>.RateLimit.hit("connection:42", :timer.minutes(1), 600)
    #=> {:allow, 1} | {:deny, retry_after_ms}

The counters live in this node's memory: with several nodes each one lets `API_RATE_LIMIT`
requests through per window. Switch `backend:` to Hammer's Redis backend
(`hammer_backend_redis`) when the limit has to hold across nodes. Each key's window starts
at its first request (`:fix_window_per_key`), so keys do not all reset at the same instant.
"""

use Hammer, backend: :ets, algorithm: :fix_window_per_key
